IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 46 to 46C: definitions of certain common phrases, citizens and aliens, the Australia Acts.
-- Every defined term of these sections has a row in tas-terms.l4; the rules here are for the definitions that have conditions, lists, dates or places in them.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- A definition worded "means" is a closed list, so a thing outside it is JUST FALSE; a definition worded "includes" is not closed, so a thing outside it is NOTHING.
-- The terms month and financial year are counted in tas-interpretation-time.l4.
-- s 46B and s 46BA are shown only as rows of dots and are not encoded.

§ `s 46: definitions of certain common phrases`

-- src:1005 | contravene includes fail to comply with;
-- src:1015 | fail to comply with includes contravene;
@ref s 46 contravene and fail to comply with (src:1005) (src:1015)
GIVEN `the expression` IS A STRING
      `the other expression` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46: the expression includes the other expression` `the expression` `the other expression` MEANS
    IF (`the expression` EQUALS "contravene" AND `the other expression` EQUALS "fail to comply with") OR (`the expression` EQUALS "fail to comply with" AND `the other expression` EQUALS "contravene")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1009 | crime shall mean an offence punishable upon indictment as provided by the Criminal Code, and where in any Act any offence is declared to be a felony or is made punishable upon information, the same shall be deemed to be a crime;
@ref s 46 crime (src:1009)
GIVEN `it is an offence punishable upon indictment as provided by the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act declares the offence to be a felony` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act makes the offence punishable upon information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the offence is a crime` `it is an offence punishable upon indictment as provided by the Criminal Code` `an Act declares the offence to be a felony` `an Act makes the offence punishable upon information` MEANS
    `it is an offence punishable upon indictment as provided by the Criminal Code` OR `an Act declares the offence to be a felony` OR `an Act makes the offence punishable upon information`

`the things an estate in land includes` MEANS LIST "estate", "interest", "easement", "right", "title", "claim", "demand", "charge", "lien", "encumbrance"

-- src:1013 | estate, used in reference to land, shall include any estate or interest, easement, right, title, claim, demand, charge, lien, or encumbrance in, over, to, or in respect of such land;
@ref s 46 estate (src:1013)
GIVEN `the expression is used in reference to land` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A STRING
      `the thing is in, over, to, or in respect of that land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46: estate includes the thing` `the expression is used in reference to land` thing `the thing is in, over, to, or in respect of that land` MEANS
    IF `the expression is used in reference to land` AND elem thing `the things an estate in land includes` AND `the thing is in, over, to, or in respect of that land`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

`the things land includes` MEANS LIST "messuages", "tenements", "hereditaments", "houses", "buildings of any tenure", "an estate or interest in land"

-- src:1037 | land shall include messuages, tenements, and hereditaments, houses, and buildings of any tenure and any estate or interest therein;
@ref s 46 land (src:1037)
GIVEN thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46: land includes the thing` thing MEANS
    IF elem thing `the things land includes` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1025 | instigate, used in relation to any offence, shall mean counsel, procure, or command;
@ref s 46 instigate (src:1025)
GIVEN `the expression is used in relation to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46: instigate means to` `the expression is used in relation to an offence` act MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the expression is used in relation to an offence`) THEN NOTHING
           IF act EQUALS "counsel" OR act EQUALS "procure" OR act EQUALS "command" THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1029 | judge means –
-- src:1031 | (a) in relation to a specified court, a judge of that court; or
-- src:1033 | (b) in any other case, a judge of the Supreme Court;
@ref s 46 judge (src:1029-1033)
GIVEN `a court is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the person is a judge` `a court is specified` `the person is a judge of that court` `the person is a judge of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF `a court is specified` THEN `the person is a judge of that court` ELSE `the person is a judge of the Supreme Court`

-- src:1039 | local authority means the council exercising jurisdiction in the locality to which the context relates;
@ref s 46 local authority (src:1039)
GIVEN `the body is the council exercising jurisdiction in the locality to which the context relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the body is the local authority` `the body is the council exercising jurisdiction in the locality to which the context relates` MEANS
    `the body is the council exercising jurisdiction in the locality to which the context relates`

-- src:1045 | mental disorder means mental illness, within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2013, arrested or incomplete development of mind, psychopathic disorder and any other disorder or disability of mind;
@ref s 46 mental disorder (src:1045)
GIVEN `it is mental illness, within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is arrested or incomplete development of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is psychopathic disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any other disorder or disability of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the condition is a mental disorder` `it is mental illness, within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2013` `it is arrested or incomplete development of mind` `it is psychopathic disorder` `it is any other disorder or disability of mind` MEANS
    `it is mental illness, within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2013` OR `it is arrested or incomplete development of mind` OR `it is psychopathic disorder` OR `it is any other disorder or disability of mind`

-- src:1065 | psychopathic disorder means a persistent disorder or disability of mind (whether or not including subnormality of intelligence) that results in abnormally aggressive or seriously irresponsible conduct on the part of a person and requires or is susceptible to medical treatment;
@ref s 46 psychopathic disorder (src:1065)
GIVEN `it is a persistent disorder or disability of mind (whether or not including subnormality of intelligence)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it results in abnormally aggressive or seriously irresponsible conduct on the part of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires or is susceptible to medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the condition is a psychopathic disorder` `it is a persistent disorder or disability of mind (whether or not including subnormality of intelligence)` `it results in abnormally aggressive or seriously irresponsible conduct on the part of a person` `it requires or is susceptible to medical treatment` MEANS
    `it is a persistent disorder or disability of mind (whether or not including subnormality of intelligence)` AND `it results in abnormally aggressive or seriously irresponsible conduct on the part of a person` AND `it requires or is susceptible to medical treatment`

-- src:1053 | offence means any contravention of, or failure to comply with, a law for which a person is liable to be punished, whether summarily or otherwise;
@ref s 46 offence (src:1053)
GIVEN `it is a contravention of, or failure to comply with, a law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person is liable to be punished for it, whether summarily or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the contravention or failure is an offence` `it is a contravention of, or failure to comply with, a law` `a person is liable to be punished for it, whether summarily or otherwise` MEANS
    `it is a contravention of, or failure to comply with, a law` AND `a person is liable to be punished for it, whether summarily or otherwise`

DECLARE `Profession under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania)` IS ONE OF
    `the medical profession`
    `the nursing profession`
    `the paramedicine profession`
    `the pharmacy profession`
    `another profession`

-- src:1043 | medical practitioner means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the medical profession;
-- src:1055 | paramedic means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the paramedicine profession;
-- src:1057 | pharmacist means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the pharmacy profession;
@ref s 46 medical practitioner, paramedic and pharmacist (src:1043) (src:1055-1057)
GIVEN `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      profession IS A `Profession under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania)`
GIVETH A `Profession under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania)`
`s 46: the person registered in the profession is a practitioner of` `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the profession` profession MEANS
    profession

-- src:1011 | enrolled nurse means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the nursing profession whose name is entered on Division 2 of the Register of Nurses, kept under that Law, as an enrolled nurse;
-- src:1069 | registered nurse means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the nursing profession whose name is entered on Division 1 of the Register of Nurses, kept under that Law, as a registered nurse;
@ref s 46 registered nurse and enrolled nurse (src:1011) (src:1069)
GIVEN `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the nursing profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division of the Register of Nurses on which the person's name is entered` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 46: the person is` `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the nursing profession` `the division of the Register of Nurses on which the person's name is entered` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Tasmania) in the nursing profession`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the division of the Register of Nurses on which the person's name is entered` EQUALS JUST 1 THEN JUST "a registered nurse"
           IF `the division of the Register of Nurses on which the person's name is entered` EQUALS JUST 2 THEN JUST "an enrolled nurse"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1067 | public place shall mean any place to which, at the relevant time, the public have access, whether on payment of money for admission thereto or otherwise;
@ref s 46 public place (src:1067)
GIVEN `the public have access to the place at the relevant time, whether on payment of money for admission or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the place is a public place` `the public have access to the place at the relevant time, whether on payment of money for admission or otherwise` MEANS
    `the public have access to the place at the relevant time, whether on payment of money for admission or otherwise`

DECLARE `Place where a declaration is made and taken` IS ONE OF
    `in this State`
    `in the United Kingdom or a British possession beyond this State`
    `in any other place`

-- src:1081 | statutory declaration or solemn declaration shall mean a declaration made and taken –
-- src:1083 | (a) in this State, in accordance with the Oaths Act 2001;
-- src:1085 | (b) in the United Kingdom or any British possession beyond this State, before a justice, notary public, or other person authorized by law to take a declaration therein;
-- src:1087 | (c) in any other place, before a British consul or vice-consul or other person having authority under any Act or Imperial Act to take a declaration;
@ref s 46 statutory declaration (src:1081-1087)
GIVEN place IS A `Place where a declaration is made and taken`
      `it is made and taken in accordance with the Oaths Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made and taken before a justice, notary public or other person authorized by law to take a declaration there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made and taken before a British consul or vice-consul or other person having authority under an Act or Imperial Act to take a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the declaration is a statutory declaration or solemn declaration` place `it is made and taken in accordance with the Oaths Act 2001` `it is made and taken before a justice, notary public or other person authorized by law to take a declaration there` `it is made and taken before a British consul or vice-consul or other person having authority under an Act or Imperial Act to take a declaration` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `in this State` THEN `it is made and taken in accordance with the Oaths Act 2001`
    WHEN `in the United Kingdom or a British possession beyond this State` THEN `it is made and taken before a justice, notary public or other person authorized by law to take a declaration there`
    WHEN `in any other place` THEN `it is made and taken before a British consul or vice-consul or other person having authority under an Act or Imperial Act to take a declaration`

-- src:1089 | Supreme Court shall mean the Supreme Court of Tasmania, and shall include the Supreme Court as first constituted under letters patent under the Great Seal of the United Kingdom, dated 13th October 1823;
@ref s 46 Supreme Court (src:1089)
GIVEN `it is the Supreme Court of Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the Supreme Court as first constituted under letters patent under the Great Seal of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of those letters patent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the court is the Supreme Court` `it is the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `it is the Supreme Court as first constituted under letters patent under the Great Seal of the United Kingdom` `the date of those letters patent` MEANS
    `it is the Supreme Court of Tasmania`
    OR (`it is the Supreme Court as first constituted under letters patent under the Great Seal of the United Kingdom` AND `the date of those letters patent` EQUALS `s 46: the date of the letters patent under the Great Seal that first constituted the Supreme Court`)

-- src:1093 | town shall mean any place proclaimed or declared to be a town under any law authorizing such proclamation or declaration;
@ref s 46 town (src:1093)
GIVEN `the place is proclaimed or declared to be a town under a law authorizing such proclamation or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46: the place is a town` `the place is proclaimed or declared to be a town under a law authorizing such proclamation or declaration` MEANS
    `the place is proclaimed or declared to be a town under a law authorizing such proclamation or declaration`

DECLARE `Document` IS ONE OF
    `a will`
    `a codicil`
    `another document`

-- src:1095 | will shall include a codicil.
@ref s 46 will (src:1095)
GIVEN document IS A `Document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46: will includes the document` document MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `a will` OR document EQUALS `a codicil` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

