§ `s 46A: references in laws of the State to Australian citizens`

DECLARE `Reference in a law of the State` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to an Australian citizen`
    `a reference to an alien`

-- src:1141 | law of the State means –
-- src:1143 | (a) an Act and any other law in force in the State;
-- src:1145 | (b) an instrument (including regulations) having effect by virtue of such an Act; and
-- src:1147 | (c) an instrument having effect by virtue of an instrument to which paragraph (b) of this definition relates.
@ref s 46A(3) law of the State (src:1141-1147)
GIVEN `it is an Act or any other law in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument (including regulations) having effect by virtue of such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument having effect by virtue of an instrument of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46A(3): the thing is a law of the State` `it is an Act or any other law in force in the State` `it is an instrument (including regulations) having effect by virtue of such an Act` `it is an instrument having effect by virtue of an instrument of that kind` MEANS
    `it is an Act or any other law in force in the State` OR `it is an instrument (including regulations) having effect by virtue of such an Act` OR `it is an instrument having effect by virtue of an instrument of that kind`

-- src:1129 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), a reference in a law of the State –
-- src:1131 | (a) to an Australian citizen, shall be read as a reference to a person who is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act; and
-- src:1133 | (b) to an alien, shall be read as a reference to a person who is not an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 46A(1) (src:1129-1133)
GIVEN `it is a law of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      reference IS A `Reference in a law of the State`
      `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` `it is a law of the State` reference `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act` MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is a law of the State`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER reference
        WHEN `a reference to an Australian citizen` THEN JUST `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act`
        WHEN `a reference to an alien` THEN JUST (NOT (`the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act`))

-- src:1135 | (2) Where a rule of law applies to or in relation to, or has effect with respect to an alien, that rule of law applies to or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, a person who is not an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 46A(2) (src:1135)
GIVEN `a rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, an alien` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46A(2): the rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, the person` `a rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, an alien` `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, an alien`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the person is an Australian citizen within the meaning of the Commonwealth Act` THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 46A(3): the thing is a law of the State` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46A(3): the thing is a law of the State` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46A(3): the thing is a law of the State` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 46A(3): the thing is a law of the State` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` TRUE `a reference to an Australian citizen` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` TRUE `a reference to an Australian citizen` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` TRUE `a reference to an alien` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` TRUE `a reference to an alien` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46A(1): the reference is read as a reference to the person` FALSE `a reference to an alien` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46A(2): the rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46A(2): the rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46A(2): the rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to, the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 46C: declaration of the effect of certain laws`

-- src:1159 | (1) In this section, written law means –
-- src:1161 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:1163 | (b) any other instrument of a legislative character.
@ref s 46C(1) (src:1159-1163)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the instrument is of a legislative character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46C(1): the thing is a written law` kind `the instrument is of a legislative character` MEANS
    kind EQUALS `an Act` OR `the instrument is of a legislative character`

-- src:1165 | (2) Each provision of a written law enacted or made or purporting to have been enacted or made before the commencement of the Australia Acts –
-- src:1167 | (a) has the same effect as it would have had; and
-- src:1169 | (b) is as valid as it would have been –
-- src:1171 | if the Australia Acts had been in force at the time of its enactment or making or purported enactment or making.
@ref s 46C(2) (src:1165-1171)
GIVEN `the day the written law was enacted or made, or purported to be enacted or made` IS A DATE
      `the day the Australia Acts commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46C(2): the provision has the same effect, and is as valid, as it would have had and been if the Australia Acts had been in force at the time` `the day the written law was enacted or made, or purported to be enacted or made` `the day the Australia Acts commenced` MEANS
    IF `s 46C(2): a written law was enacted or made before the commencement of the Australia Acts` `the day the written law was enacted or made, or purported to be enacted or made` `with` `the day the Australia Acts commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The text gives no day for the commencement of the Australia Acts; the day in these tests (3 March 1986) is a fixture chosen for the tests.
#ASSERT `s 46C(1): the thing is a written law` `an Act` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46C(1): the thing is a written law` `a regulation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 46C(1): the thing is a written law` `an order` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 46C(2): the provision has the same effect, and is as valid, as it would have had and been if the Australia Acts had been in force at the time` (Date 1 1 1980) (Date 3 3 1986) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46C(2): the provision has the same effect, and is as valid, as it would have had and been if the Australia Acts had been in force at the time` (Date 3 3 1986) (Date 3 3 1986) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46C(2): the provision has the same effect, and is as valid, as it would have had and been if the Australia Acts had been in force at the time` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 3 3 1986) EQUALS NOTHING
